Package: mcp-python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, adduser, bash
Recommends: coreutils
Description: MCP server - runs a Python 3 code at the host.
 Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, over Streamable HTTP (HTTP, HTTPS or
 both), with tools to run a Python 3 code, submitted by an MCP client, in
 a fresh interpreter process.
 .
 The server Python packages are installed at the package configuration,
 into a virtual environment of the host 'python3', from the Python package
 index pip is configured for - the exact set of 'requirements.lock'. The
 configuration - '/etc/mcp-python/mcp-python.conf', the service -
 'mcp-python.service'. Authentication - a bearer token per client, see
 'mcp-python-token'; no clients after the installation. 'shred'
 (coreutils) overwrites the token files at a purge.
